WEBVTT

1
00:00:31.080 --> 00:00:33.600
There are no records of us.

2
00:00:33.680 --> 00:00:36.760
No birth records, no fingerprints.

3
00:00:37.040 --> 00:00:38.920
All records are empty.

4
00:00:39.720 --> 00:00:44.240
People call us 'Empty Shells' saying
we're empty inside.

5
00:00:44.400 --> 00:00:46.120
That's why searches turn up blank.

6
00:00:46.800 --> 00:00:47.840
Very interesting.

7
00:00:48.400 --> 00:00:53.120
So the accident on December
24 was the start of everything?

8
00:00:54.960 --> 00:00:57.440
The bus skidded by chance.

9
00:00:58.200 --> 00:00:59.360
Christmas Eve.

10
00:00:59.560 --> 00:01:01.400
It was supposed to be a joyous day,

11
00:01:01.480 --> 00:01:02.840
but tragedy struck.

12
00:01:02.960 --> 00:01:05.320
And people died by chance.

13
00:01:05.400 --> 00:01:09.480
The bus did not slow down and
drove across the crosswalk.

14
00:01:10.080 --> 00:01:12.600
It was confirmed there was
nothing wrong with the vehicle.

15
00:01:12.840 --> 00:01:16.760
It was concluded that black ice
on the road was to blame.

16
00:01:16.960 --> 00:01:20.040
"A tragic accident on Christmas Eve."

17
00:01:20.400 --> 00:01:22.560
That was the news headline.

18
00:01:23.080 --> 00:01:25.320
The bus hit a man,

19
00:01:25.560 --> 00:01:28.360
who had no records under his name.

20
00:01:28.520 --> 00:01:30.480
He was also an Empty Shell.

21
00:01:31.120 --> 00:01:34.040
That's how Odd Eye died.

22
00:01:34.480 --> 00:01:36.280
How close are you two?

23
00:01:36.480 --> 00:01:38.840
He's the only person who believed me.

24
00:01:39.080 --> 00:01:41.080
He has different vision in each eye.

25
00:01:41.400 --> 00:01:43.440
So I named him Odd Eye.

26
00:01:43.600 --> 00:01:46.920
Why do you think Odd Eye was killed?

27
00:01:47.000 --> 00:01:49.560
Odd Eye didn't die by accident.

28
00:01:49.760 --> 00:01:52.520
All accidents can be plotted.

29
00:01:52.640 --> 00:01:54.200
Plotted accidents?

30
00:01:54.520 --> 00:01:56.440
That's what we do.

31
00:01:59.560 --> 00:02:06.120
The Plot

32
00:02:06.800 --> 00:02:08.320
There's been an accident.

33
00:02:08.400 --> 00:02:10.720
I don't know. A truck's turned over.

34
00:02:10.880 --> 00:02:12.440
Just hang onto those guys.

35
00:02:12.520 --> 00:02:15.320
Trust me, those rich idiots
will invest in anything.

36
00:02:15.520 --> 00:02:17.120
Don't screw it up by opening your mouth.

37
00:02:17.200 --> 00:02:19.200
Just keep them there for me.

38
00:02:19.280 --> 00:02:21.680
And get rid of anyone
trying to mooch off them.

39
00:02:21.760 --> 00:02:22.760
Yeah.

40
00:02:23.080 --> 00:02:24.640
What's taking so long?

41
00:02:25.640 --> 00:02:26.800
Hey! You little...!

42
00:02:27.200 --> 00:02:30.000
No, not you.

43
00:02:31.080 --> 00:02:32.560
Hey, asshole!

44
00:02:37.440 --> 00:02:39.360
That little shit.

45
00:02:41.560 --> 00:02:44.480
Stop flashing your lights and wait.

46
00:02:45.520 --> 00:02:48.400
Come on. Let's go, let's go.

47
00:02:49.480 --> 00:02:51.440
Give me a break.

48
00:02:57.240 --> 00:02:58.400
Damn it.

49
00:03:04.800 --> 00:03:07.080
That's a big load you're pulling.

50
00:03:07.600 --> 00:03:10.040
You're in everyone's way, lady.

51
00:03:12.880 --> 00:03:13.960
What is it?

52
00:03:14.080 --> 00:03:15.360
I said I'm on my way.

53
00:03:15.480 --> 00:03:18.680
This delivery guy was pissing me off.

54
00:03:19.120 --> 00:03:20.360
Wow, look at that...

55
00:03:27.200 --> 00:03:30.720
You dumb shit! Stop calling me
and just keep them there!

56
00:03:31.920 --> 00:03:34.560
You better keep them there!

57
00:03:39.840 --> 00:03:41.280
It's that bastard from before.

58
00:03:41.600 --> 00:03:43.120
I'm gonna kill him.

59
00:03:48.400 --> 00:03:50.440
Dammit, that little prick!

60
00:04:06.360 --> 00:04:07.360
Shit!

61
00:04:07.880 --> 00:04:09.320
There should be a sign here!

62
00:04:10.880 --> 00:04:12.800
Hey! Hey!

63
00:04:21.240 --> 00:04:24.760
Hey! Who's in charge?! Come out!

64
00:04:25.400 --> 00:04:26.080
Yes?

65
00:04:26.280 --> 00:04:28.720
Are you in charge? Get down here.

66
00:04:29.120 --> 00:04:29.800
Why?

67
00:04:30.040 --> 00:04:34.400
Why? You see this paint
and you're asking why?

68
00:04:34.760 --> 00:04:36.160
Don't throw a fit.

69
00:04:37.160 --> 00:04:39.040
What the...

70
00:04:40.600 --> 00:04:42.000
Shit.

71
00:04:59.960 --> 00:05:01.640
That scared me.

72
00:05:40.360 --> 00:05:42.000
Out of the way. Move, please!

73
00:05:42.080 --> 00:05:43.760
Over here. This way!

74
00:05:43.880 --> 00:05:44.400
Hurry, hurry!

75
00:05:44.440 --> 00:05:45.200
He's over here.

76
00:05:45.280 --> 00:05:47.240
Sir.

77
00:05:48.320 --> 00:05:49.800
I am a paramedic. Sir!

78
00:05:51.160 --> 00:05:53.480
How long has it been?

79
00:05:53.520 --> 00:05:56.520
About 15 minutes... He's been unconscious.

80
00:05:58.360 --> 00:06:01.160
There's no pulse. Call the precinct.

81
00:06:04.440 --> 00:06:05.520
Disengage.

82
00:06:07.280 --> 00:06:09.160
Due to demolition work
in redevelopment areas

83
00:06:09.240 --> 00:06:13.240
there have been several accidents
involving old buildings.

84
00:06:13.480 --> 00:06:18.600
This is the fourth accident due
to careless management.

85
00:06:18.680 --> 00:06:22.440
There was a building collapse
in Gwangjin-go today.

86
00:06:22.720 --> 00:06:25.040
Park, in his 40s, died on the spot.

87
00:06:25.080 --> 00:06:27.360
This delivery guy was pissing me off.

88
00:06:27.680 --> 00:06:29.040
Wow, look at that...

89
00:06:35.280 --> 00:06:37.120
According to officials at the site

90
00:06:37.280 --> 00:06:40.800
strong wind warnings were ignored,
and the demolition work continued.

91
00:06:42.760 --> 00:06:43.960
Are you in charge?

92
00:06:44.040 --> 00:06:44.800
Why?

93
00:06:44.880 --> 00:06:47.120
Why? You see this paint
and you're asking why?

94
00:06:47.280 --> 00:06:48.480
Don't throw a fit.

95
00:06:54.280 --> 00:06:58.840
This afternoon in Gwangjin district,
a truck turned over

96
00:06:58.920 --> 00:07:02.320
causing congestion in the area.

97
00:07:04.160 --> 00:07:05.800
What's taking so long?

98
00:07:06.800 --> 00:07:07.800
Hey! You little...!

99
00:07:21.680 --> 00:07:24.080
That's a big load you're pulling.

100
00:07:39.040 --> 00:07:41.640
Dammit, that little prick!

101
00:08:01.320 --> 00:08:02.840
The job is done.

102
00:08:04.200 --> 00:08:06.320
Please leave the money in the car.

103
00:08:32.400 --> 00:08:33.520
Good work, everyone.

104
00:08:33.600 --> 00:08:34.720
Welcome back.

105
00:08:37.120 --> 00:08:39.480
What should I do now?

106
00:08:41.600 --> 00:08:45.040
Need my help? Should
we sort out the phones?

107
00:08:46.600 --> 00:08:50.560
With no experience as a prosecutor,
the nominee is drawing attention.

108
00:08:50.680 --> 00:08:53.960
Meanwhile at 1 p.m. today there
was a tower crane accident.

109
00:08:54.000 --> 00:08:57.720
The CEO of Yangseon Construction,
Kim Han-jin, was killed,

110
00:08:57.840 --> 00:09:01.200
and his younger brother
Kim Doo-jin narrowly escaped...

111
00:09:01.560 --> 00:09:04.560
There were two more casualties,
leading to a total of three.

112
00:09:04.640 --> 00:09:05.720
Jackie, look.

113
00:09:05.920 --> 00:09:07.056
The police are looking into the accident.

114
00:09:07.080 --> 00:09:08.360
This accident...

115
00:09:09.080 --> 00:09:10.120
Isn't it suspicious?

116
00:09:12.480 --> 00:09:16.080
A crane fell, but only
Kim Doo-jin survived.

117
00:09:17.280 --> 00:09:19.600
And he takes charge of the company?

118
00:09:20.120 --> 00:09:21.880
Wol-cheon... That's too clichéd.

119
00:09:22.680 --> 00:09:25.440
Kim Doo-jin is currently being treated
in the hospital,

120
00:09:25.520 --> 00:09:29.800
and the public is waiting for
the company to release a statement.

121
00:09:31.760 --> 00:09:34.480
An accident that was
intended is not coincidence.

122
00:09:35.880 --> 00:09:37.280
Two additional deaths.

123
00:09:38.200 --> 00:09:40.280
Also, there were additional deaths.

124
00:09:40.360 --> 00:09:41.000
This...

125
00:09:41.160 --> 00:09:43.280
was made to look like an accident.

126
00:09:44.800 --> 00:09:46.360
The target, Kim Han-jin.

127
00:09:46.520 --> 00:09:47.960
The client, Kim Doo-jin.

128
00:09:49.040 --> 00:09:52.560
Only the Sweepers are
capable of something on this scale.

129
00:09:53.000 --> 00:09:55.280
What are the Sweepers?

130
00:09:55.400 --> 00:09:58.480
If we're a small family business,
they're a conglomerate.

131
00:10:00.440 --> 00:10:04.640
If we worked there, Wol-cheon could
afford to become a woman.

132
00:10:06.360 --> 00:10:08.080
They're like ghosts. Forget it.

133
00:10:08.200 --> 00:10:10.376
You can tell just by looking
at the news reports, can't you?

134
00:10:10.400 --> 00:10:12.360
Have you ever seen the Sweepers?

135
00:10:12.560 --> 00:10:14.280
I haven't, but...
Welcome back!

136
00:10:14.520 --> 00:10:15.760
Good job, everyone.

137
00:10:19.920 --> 00:10:22.720
Jeom-man, how was it?
It was your first time today.

138
00:10:22.800 --> 00:10:24.080
No problem.

139
00:10:27.120 --> 00:10:28.240
You sure you're okay?

140
00:10:28.760 --> 00:10:30.160
I am definitely sure.

141
00:10:30.600 --> 00:10:34.120
Better to be afraid. So
you don't make mistakes.

142
00:10:34.480 --> 00:10:38.160
There were additional deaths.
Don't you find that strange?

143
00:10:38.280 --> 00:10:41.360
That's what accidents are like.
Natural and ruthless.

144
00:10:41.640 --> 00:10:44.040
Those who have been through war know.

145
00:10:44.440 --> 00:10:46.520
You just miss the meth, don't you?

146
00:10:46.640 --> 00:10:48.160
Not meth, morphine.

147
00:10:48.240 --> 00:10:50.640
In Vietnam, morphine was legal.

148
00:10:51.320 --> 00:10:53.360
It was a rational choice to forget the war.

149
00:10:53.440 --> 00:10:55.240
Enough with the Vietnam talk.

150
00:10:55.320 --> 00:10:57.240
I think our incident has gone well.

151
00:10:58.240 --> 00:11:00.560
In the news, they're only talking
about Kim Han-jin.

152
00:11:00.720 --> 00:11:01.720
That's good.

153
00:11:02.160 --> 00:11:04.120
Accidents cover up accidents.

154
00:11:04.960 --> 00:11:06.280
The Kim Han-jin incident...

155
00:11:08.400 --> 00:11:09.800
It's the Sweepers.

156
00:11:09.960 --> 00:11:11.320
Right, you think so too?

157
00:11:11.360 --> 00:11:12.760
Jackie, what did I tell you?

158
00:11:12.840 --> 00:11:14.440
What do you think, Jackie?

159
00:11:15.200 --> 00:11:17.400
You still think the Sweepers don't exist?

160
00:11:19.560 --> 00:11:21.480
We only believe what we see.

161
00:11:26.320 --> 00:11:28.360
Then who killed Odd Eye?

162
00:11:30.080 --> 00:11:32.120
You still believe his
death was an accident?

163
00:11:40.800 --> 00:11:43.200
The Sweepers have surfaced
for the first time in a year.

164
00:11:45.080 --> 00:11:46.840
They'll surely strike again.

165
00:11:49.600 --> 00:11:52.000
We can't fall victim to them again.

166
00:12:01.040 --> 00:12:03.280
So, who is Odd Eye?

167
00:12:03.960 --> 00:12:05.400
Someone dear to me.

168
00:12:15.280 --> 00:12:17.440
Jackie, do you hear me?

169
00:12:17.600 --> 00:12:19.016
He built this business with Young-il.

170
00:12:19.040 --> 00:12:20.280
You're shaking...

171
00:12:20.440 --> 00:12:25.280
Young-il made the plans,
and Odd Eye took care of the rest.

172
00:12:25.520 --> 00:12:27.320
Young-il does everything now.

173
00:12:27.560 --> 00:12:29.040
Jackie, just get it together.

174
00:12:34.160 --> 00:12:35.400
She'll do it again.

175
00:12:35.800 --> 00:12:37.720
She said this is the last time.

176
00:12:38.760 --> 00:12:39.800
Right, Jackie?

177
00:12:40.080 --> 00:12:42.320
Those were the days...

178
00:12:42.400 --> 00:12:45.560
Jackie, you're our family.
So, we keep our promises.

179
00:12:45.760 --> 00:12:47.080
Right?

180
00:12:59.680 --> 00:13:01.440
Odd Eye gave me this.

181
00:13:01.680 --> 00:13:03.160
Sweet kid.

182
00:13:03.840 --> 00:13:06.120
He said quit everything
else and just smoke this.

183
00:13:07.360 --> 00:13:10.880
If it wasn't for Odd Eye,
I'd be resting in eternal peace.

184
00:13:11.280 --> 00:13:13.800
But why'd the Sweepers kill him?

185
00:13:14.000 --> 00:13:15.840
One day, Young-il said,

186
00:13:16.680 --> 00:13:18.720
"The Sweepers killed Odd Eye."

187
00:13:19.040 --> 00:13:20.800
That's all I heard.

188
00:13:21.240 --> 00:13:24.160
He was an Empty Shell,
so I couldn't look him up either.

189
00:13:24.680 --> 00:13:25.920
Why not?

190
00:13:26.120 --> 00:13:29.480
With no birth record,
there's no death record.

191
00:13:30.280 --> 00:13:33.520
Only Young-il knows the truth.

192
00:13:34.200 --> 00:13:36.840
Does that mean they could kill us too?

193
00:13:38.400 --> 00:13:40.360
Why? You scared?

194
00:13:40.880 --> 00:13:44.440
I've seen things, too.
This doesn't scare me.

195
00:13:45.040 --> 00:13:45.960
Seen things, where?

196
00:13:46.040 --> 00:13:47.640
I've been to the joint.

197
00:13:48.080 --> 00:13:49.520
Don't underestimate me.

198
00:13:50.560 --> 00:13:52.000
Gosh, I'm scared.

199
00:13:54.640 --> 00:13:57.840
Girl, stop changing
clothes. It's distracting.

200
00:13:58.400 --> 00:14:00.120
Gotta do what I gotta do.

201
00:14:01.280 --> 00:14:03.920
What are you staring at? Eyes on the road!

202
00:14:05.960 --> 00:14:07.800
She's touchy today.

203
00:14:07.920 --> 00:14:10.360
Enough talk of the dead, already.

204
00:14:10.520 --> 00:14:12.160
Aren't you sick of talking about Odd Eye?

205
00:14:15.880 --> 00:14:18.600
We've thrown 3 away in
Gangnam, so let's go north.

206
00:14:18.840 --> 00:14:20.480
Can't we just toss it here?

207
00:14:20.560 --> 00:14:22.880
Hey, trash can become evidence.

208
00:14:22.960 --> 00:14:24.480
Evidence leads to a case.

209
00:14:24.680 --> 00:14:25.680
Just keep going.

210
00:14:26.160 --> 00:14:28.240
Save the polar bears.
Think of climate change...

211
00:14:28.520 --> 00:14:29.760
I'm sorry.

212
00:14:31.920 --> 00:14:34.480
For the sake of the Earth, please help.

213
00:14:47.920 --> 00:14:50.000
If I see you have a
companion, I'll hang up.

214
00:14:50.160 --> 00:14:52.480
If you don't reply within 10 seconds,
I'll hang up.

215
00:14:52.520 --> 00:14:54.560
If you give me wrong
information, I'll hang up.

216
00:14:55.720 --> 00:14:56.720
Yes.

217
00:14:56.920 --> 00:14:58.040
Keep walking.

218
00:14:59.120 --> 00:15:01.160
You have the deposit and documents?

219
00:15:01.320 --> 00:15:04.320
Yes, I have the ID card and certificates.

220
00:15:04.400 --> 00:15:05.800
And the bank account details?

221
00:15:06.400 --> 00:15:08.040
Yes. I have that too.

222
00:15:08.320 --> 00:15:09.560
Turn right.

223
00:15:13.240 --> 00:15:14.400
The target name?

224
00:15:15.000 --> 00:15:16.480
Joo Sung-jik.

225
00:15:16.640 --> 00:15:18.000
How old is the target?

226
00:15:19.200 --> 00:15:20.440
63 years old.

227
00:15:20.960 --> 00:15:22.200
And your relationship to him?

228
00:15:25.840 --> 00:15:27.600
Do you need to know that?

229
00:15:27.680 --> 00:15:30.360
The closer the relationship,
the higher the fee.

230
00:15:33.640 --> 00:15:34.920
He's my father.

231
00:15:36.440 --> 00:15:37.720
Keep walking.

232
00:15:39.280 --> 00:15:40.960
You see that trash can?

233
00:15:43.040 --> 00:15:45.320
Put your documents in the envelope.

234
00:15:52.920 --> 00:15:54.880
Throw it in the trash can.

235
00:16:03.440 --> 00:16:06.200
I'll call you after
reviewing the documents.

236
00:16:44.440 --> 00:16:47.560
Agatha Christie's
novel 'Death on the Nile'.

237
00:16:47.640 --> 00:16:49.640
This was the introduction to today's book.

238
00:16:49.800 --> 00:16:51.440
I'll come back after listening to a song.

239
00:17:04.920 --> 00:17:08.960
Joo Sung-jik has been nominated
as the next Prosecutor General.

240
00:17:09.200 --> 00:17:14.720
However, his daughter faces
allegations of hiding a slush fund.

241
00:17:14.760 --> 00:17:17.000
Joo has denied everything,

242
00:17:17.120 --> 00:17:21.200
but the money is said to have
been raised by his wife Lee Hwa-sun,

243
00:17:21.240 --> 00:17:24.720
who died in a traffic
accident three years ago.

244
00:17:39.440 --> 00:17:43.200
This is the site of the fatal accident.

245
00:17:43.480 --> 00:17:45.800
After the bus ran over Ms. Lee...

246
00:17:46.800 --> 00:17:51.840
Due to his wife's death, the investigation
into Joo's finances has stalled.

247
00:17:51.920 --> 00:17:53.960
The prosecution has suspended questioning,

248
00:17:54.000 --> 00:17:56.280
and Joo is expected to
keep his Assembly seat.

249
00:17:56.440 --> 00:18:01.280
Pedestrians were also hit,
so three people in total were killed.

250
00:18:01.600 --> 00:18:06.680
It took place at an intersection,
in the middle of the crosswalk.

251
00:18:06.760 --> 00:18:12.080
Belongings strewn on the
road depict the tragic situation.

252
00:18:12.360 --> 00:18:14.400
There were no vehicle defects.

253
00:18:14.480 --> 00:18:19.320
The police are looking into why
the bus drove into the crosswalk.

254
00:18:29.240 --> 00:18:30.800
It's just like with Odd Eye.

255
00:18:32.000 --> 00:18:33.240
The cause unclear.

256
00:18:34.160 --> 00:18:35.560
Three deaths.

257
00:18:40.560 --> 00:18:42.040
This is the Sweepers' doing.

258
00:18:44.560 --> 00:18:46.120
The target was Lee Hwa-sun.

259
00:18:48.680 --> 00:18:50.080
And the client, her husband.

260
00:18:50.680 --> 00:18:54.840
Suspicions over Lee's illicit funds
have surfaced once again.

261
00:18:55.160 --> 00:19:01.040
We expect Joo Sung-jik's daughter,
Joo Young, to be investigated.

262
00:19:02.440 --> 00:19:04.840
He'll hire the Sweepers again.

263
00:19:05.920 --> 00:19:07.640
We can catch them.

264
00:19:10.440 --> 00:19:16.720
Joo's daughter is alleged to have received
her mother's slush fund.

265
00:19:16.960 --> 00:19:20.560
Joo Young may be brought
in by the prosecution.

266
00:19:20.720 --> 00:19:23.120
Young-il, look at this.

267
00:19:29.520 --> 00:19:32.720
Due to this accident, one policeman died,

268
00:19:33.080 --> 00:19:35.320
and a policeman in the passenger
seat was hospitalized...

269
00:19:35.360 --> 00:19:36.360
This accident...

270
00:19:37.600 --> 00:19:38.840
It's the Sweepers, right?

271
00:19:39.720 --> 00:19:41.240
That accident was plotted.

272
00:19:42.360 --> 00:19:43.920
It's just like you said.

273
00:19:45.360 --> 00:19:46.920
Why are the Sweepers after us?

274
00:19:47.360 --> 00:19:49.880
Wouldn't it be stranger
if no one was after us?

275
00:19:50.000 --> 00:19:52.520
The client, people around the target...
Could be anyone.

276
00:19:52.600 --> 00:19:53.880
I'll sort it out.

277
00:19:56.160 --> 00:19:57.400
Just trust me.

278
00:20:00.720 --> 00:20:02.200
The food is here.

279
00:20:05.280 --> 00:20:07.680
What's this?
Burgers. From a place I like.

280
00:20:08.520 --> 00:20:09.600
Jeom-man...

281
00:20:09.880 --> 00:20:12.280
You think we work our
butts off just to eat burgers?

282
00:20:12.400 --> 00:20:14.080
What's wrong with burgers?

283
00:20:14.680 --> 00:20:17.560
A Rwandan coffee and a croissant
would be perfect about now.

284
00:20:18.400 --> 00:20:19.400
What's that?

285
00:20:20.440 --> 00:20:21.680
Like I would know?

286
00:20:21.720 --> 00:20:25.080
I didn't think our little Jeommy would
have such common taste.

287
00:20:27.720 --> 00:20:29.440
There're two left...
I'm okay.

288
00:20:30.360 --> 00:20:31.400
Okay.

289
00:20:35.120 --> 00:20:36.480
So why's the daughter doing this?

290
00:20:37.160 --> 00:20:40.920
They're probing her dead mom.
Wouldn't you be pissed?

291
00:20:41.000 --> 00:20:43.360
Who wouldn't, with this racket...

292
00:20:43.720 --> 00:20:46.280
It'd all end if her dad
just gave up the nomination.

293
00:20:46.720 --> 00:20:47.880
He won't give it up.

294
00:20:48.480 --> 00:20:50.480
It was the same situation with his wife,

295
00:20:50.600 --> 00:20:52.000
but he just kept going.

296
00:20:52.320 --> 00:20:55.600
I apologize for causing public concern.

297
00:20:55.840 --> 00:20:59.760
Today, I reported my wife
to the prosecution myself.

298
00:21:00.040 --> 00:21:03.720
If the charges are proven true,
she'll be punished by law.

299
00:21:03.800 --> 00:21:07.600
Wow, he's shameless.
Only cares about himself.

300
00:21:07.920 --> 00:21:09.016
I will announce my stance...

301
00:21:09.040 --> 00:21:11.040
Joo's fame bothers me.

302
00:21:11.640 --> 00:21:14.600
The more eyes on him,
the more we risk being exposed.

303
00:21:14.800 --> 00:21:16.160
The more eyes on him,

304
00:21:16.960 --> 00:21:18.600
the more who'll believe it's an accident.

305
00:21:18.640 --> 00:21:20.600
We've never done a job this big.

306
00:21:21.400 --> 00:21:24.200
Wait, his wife's death is a bit strange.

307
00:21:24.520 --> 00:21:27.240
A bus accident, two other deaths...

308
00:21:27.520 --> 00:21:29.040
Young-il, isn't it suspicious?

309
00:21:30.880 --> 00:21:33.040
Anyone who's nervous can skip this job.

310
00:21:33.360 --> 00:21:35.120
If you're in, so am I. You?

311
00:21:35.200 --> 00:21:37.240
I'm in! I need the money.

312
00:21:41.520 --> 00:21:42.920
Jackie, say something.

313
00:21:47.760 --> 00:21:50.120
Jackie, I need you and
your experience for this job.

314
00:21:52.800 --> 00:21:53.840
You need me...?

315
00:21:56.320 --> 00:21:59.440
I've always preferred hearing that
over "I love you".

316
00:21:59.720 --> 00:22:01.360
So I guess I'm in.

317
00:22:01.600 --> 00:22:02.600
Let's do it.

318
00:22:06.040 --> 00:22:07.200
Let's start with a diagnosis.

319
00:22:28.920 --> 00:22:30.800
Hey, Jeom-man. You're on.

320
00:22:31.520 --> 00:22:32.920
On where?

321
00:22:33.560 --> 00:22:34.560
Live news.

322
00:22:35.280 --> 00:22:36.280
Live news?

323
00:22:39.240 --> 00:22:40.400
Are you crazy?

324
00:22:40.480 --> 00:22:41.760
I'm so sorry.

325
00:22:41.960 --> 00:22:43.040
Keep your distance.

326
00:22:43.120 --> 00:22:44.800
Yes, sir.

327
00:22:44.880 --> 00:22:46.360
How about we keep it simple?

328
00:22:46.480 --> 00:22:47.480
Tell me more.

329
00:22:47.560 --> 00:22:49.400
They drive at the same time each day,

330
00:22:49.480 --> 00:22:51.320
so how about a traffic accident?

331
00:22:52.120 --> 00:22:54.760
The faster they go, the
higher the fatality rate.

332
00:22:55.880 --> 00:22:58.680
Falling objects cause
over 1000 accidents a year.

333
00:23:00.760 --> 00:23:01.880
Or the leaf spring?

334
00:23:03.520 --> 00:23:04.880
It'll seem plausible.

335
00:23:07.920 --> 00:23:09.560
Could put the client at risk.

336
00:23:10.360 --> 00:23:11.120
I guess so.

337
00:23:11.320 --> 00:23:12.320
Jeommy!

338
00:23:12.520 --> 00:23:14.280
Work your brain. Give
us something dazzling.

339
00:23:14.640 --> 00:23:15.640
Something dazzling...

340
00:23:16.560 --> 00:23:17.840
You mean big, right?

341
00:23:18.040 --> 00:23:20.360
I like big. Keep talking.

342
00:23:20.840 --> 00:23:22.120
A rollover accident?

343
00:23:22.200 --> 00:23:23.320
You're too nice.

344
00:23:24.680 --> 00:23:26.840
Let's try something
besides traffic accidents.

345
00:23:27.560 --> 00:23:28.960
Something static.

346
00:23:29.880 --> 00:23:33.120
Since dawn, I've been waiting
for Joo Sung-jik to arrive.

347
00:23:33.200 --> 00:23:35.880
I bet they'll summon Joo Young this week.

348
00:23:35.960 --> 00:23:37.480
Along with her mother's slush fund...

349
00:23:37.520 --> 00:23:40.200
But you never know. They could
be in cahoots with the prosecutors.

350
00:23:40.240 --> 00:23:41.760
The early bird gets the worm...

351
00:23:41.840 --> 00:23:43.200
It's him! In the SM5!

352
00:23:43.280 --> 00:23:44.560
Joo Sung-jik has arrived.

353
00:23:44.640 --> 00:23:46.360
Whether he'll open his mouth...

354
00:23:48.000 --> 00:23:51.680
Hey! Stop pushing! Out of the way!

355
00:23:51.800 --> 00:23:53.360
I said don't push!

356
00:23:53.520 --> 00:23:55.360
Is it true about your slush fund?

357
00:23:55.440 --> 00:23:57.960
All he needs to do is
give up the nomination...

358
00:23:58.080 --> 00:23:59.800
It's chaos here!

359
00:23:59.840 --> 00:24:01.040
She's so pretty.

360
00:24:15.120 --> 00:24:16.920
It's connected. Move out.

361
00:24:17.880 --> 00:24:19.120
I'm done here.

362
00:24:24.320 --> 00:24:25.720
How about jumping off the building?

363
00:24:27.160 --> 00:24:28.680
Right on top of the reporters?

364
00:24:30.680 --> 00:24:33.120
The motive is clear
and it's safe for the client.

365
00:24:36.360 --> 00:24:37.520
Like Leslie Cheung?

366
00:24:37.600 --> 00:24:40.680
Suicide on April Fool's
Day. An ironic tragedy.

367
00:24:40.880 --> 00:24:43.720
How's he supposed to climb
over the guardrail with his legs?

368
00:24:43.840 --> 00:24:44.880
Ah, sorry.

369
00:24:45.040 --> 00:24:47.160
I just had a great idea!

370
00:24:47.360 --> 00:24:49.120
Drop an air conditioner unit on his head!

371
00:24:49.200 --> 00:24:51.520
What about the big roof above the entrance?

372
00:24:53.960 --> 00:24:55.200
It goes through the roof?

373
00:24:56.120 --> 00:24:57.160
You're so cute.

374
00:24:58.120 --> 00:24:59.880
Young-il! I got an idea.

375
00:24:59.960 --> 00:25:03.280
Jackie, anything else?

376
00:25:06.200 --> 00:25:09.560
Electrocution is the best.

377
00:25:09.920 --> 00:25:11.560
You'll barbecue them both?

378
00:25:11.880 --> 00:25:13.120
We can separate them.

379
00:25:13.680 --> 00:25:14.800
How?

380
00:25:19.080 --> 00:25:21.080
I'm not taking calls from reporters.

381
00:25:22.080 --> 00:25:23.120
Joo Young!

382
00:25:24.400 --> 00:25:26.000
I told you to take the calls.

383
00:25:26.160 --> 00:25:28.160
I was busy with something.

384
00:25:28.840 --> 00:25:31.920
Don't show any emotion or expression.

385
00:25:33.000 --> 00:25:34.280
Let's chew over it a bit more.

386
00:25:35.360 --> 00:25:39.000
Don't worry. It'll all work out.

387
00:25:46.720 --> 00:25:49.880
Hold on. There's a tip that Joo Young
was bullied in school.

388
00:25:49.960 --> 00:25:53.440
Not because she was
pretty. She had spasms...

389
00:25:53.560 --> 00:25:55.000
Epileptic spasms?

390
00:25:55.080 --> 00:25:57.080
Something like this.

391
00:25:57.360 --> 00:25:59.680
She'll probably use it as an excuse
to skip questioning.

392
00:25:59.800 --> 00:26:01.616
Joo Sung-jik has come out!
I'll ask him a question.

393
00:26:01.640 --> 00:26:02.760
He's here!

394
00:26:11.200 --> 00:26:13.560
Jeom-man, what is this?
A collection of random heads?

395
00:26:13.760 --> 00:26:15.280
There are good shots too.

396
00:26:15.840 --> 00:26:18.080
The camera flashes are crazy.

397
00:26:18.520 --> 00:26:21.680
Must be hard being famous.
I couldn't open my eyes.

398
00:26:22.200 --> 00:26:23.400
How did Joo Young react?

399
00:26:23.480 --> 00:26:25.760
She just squinted her eyes.

400
00:26:25.840 --> 00:26:27.880
Stop pushing!

401
00:26:30.360 --> 00:26:31.880
Princess Diana died like that.

402
00:26:31.960 --> 00:26:33.280
Didn't she die in a car crash?

403
00:26:33.440 --> 00:26:35.840
The paparazzi hounded
her right to her death.

404
00:26:36.040 --> 00:26:38.360
The ambulance came
40 minutes after the crash.

405
00:26:38.440 --> 00:26:39.680
Why was the ambulance late?

406
00:26:39.760 --> 00:26:43.000
You really think the paparazzi called
the ambulance?

407
00:26:43.720 --> 00:26:46.640
If you look closely, it wasn't an accident.

408
00:26:46.720 --> 00:26:48.640
You mean the ambulance was in on it?

409
00:26:48.680 --> 00:26:51.160
Not the ambulance, but the paparazzi.

410
00:26:51.440 --> 00:26:52.960
He just pretended to call.

411
00:26:53.800 --> 00:26:54.640
Wow.

412
00:26:54.680 --> 00:26:57.080
Do you know how the
Vietcong beat the Americans?

413
00:26:57.240 --> 00:26:58.320
America lost?

414
00:26:59.440 --> 00:27:03.360
The Method. How much
can you think like the Yanks?

415
00:27:03.600 --> 00:27:05.120
That decided the outcome.

416
00:27:05.720 --> 00:27:08.120
How much can you think like Joo Sung-jik?

417
00:27:08.240 --> 00:27:10.240
How can he be killed?

418
00:27:12.120 --> 00:27:14.360
Why live with someone
until you want to kill them?

419
00:27:15.080 --> 00:27:16.280
It's absurd.

420
00:27:16.400 --> 00:27:18.480
She's killing him because
she has no way out.

421
00:27:20.080 --> 00:27:21.320
There's no way out.

422
00:27:23.600 --> 00:27:26.040
Joo and his daughter are always together.

423
00:27:27.680 --> 00:27:29.040
Need to get them apart.

424
00:27:29.840 --> 00:27:32.080
The camera flashes are crazy.

425
00:27:32.400 --> 00:27:33.800
The people's eyes become a weapon.

426
00:27:33.880 --> 00:27:36.120
She just squinted her eyes.

427
00:27:37.160 --> 00:27:38.160
And excitement...

428
00:27:40.400 --> 00:27:41.920
causes an accident.

429
00:27:53.880 --> 00:27:54.920
Let's wait for the rain.

430
00:27:55.760 --> 00:27:56.760
The rain?

431
00:27:57.120 --> 00:27:58.680
This is Hauser.

432
00:27:58.800 --> 00:28:00.880
Have you heard of Mothman?

433
00:28:01.400 --> 00:28:05.880
The creature with moth wings that
appears in times of disaster.

434
00:28:06.000 --> 00:28:09.120
It appeared at Chernobyl
and the 9/11 attacks.

435
00:28:09.360 --> 00:28:12.880
Mothman will appear in the middle of Korea.

436
00:28:12.920 --> 00:28:14.680
Let me predict the future.

437
00:28:16.080 --> 00:28:17.840
Joo Sung-jik will die soon.

438
00:28:18.440 --> 00:28:21.920
And Mothman will show
up at the place he dies.

439
00:28:22.680 --> 00:28:26.120
A guy on the internet named Hauser
said Joo Sung-jik will die soon.

440
00:28:26.640 --> 00:28:30.080
If he does die, this guy will
get 10,000 subscribers.

441
00:28:30.960 --> 00:28:33.680
Shouldn't we get paid by him, then?

442
00:28:38.800 --> 00:28:39.800
Jeom-man?

443
00:28:42.280 --> 00:28:43.280
Jeom-man?

444
00:28:45.160 --> 00:28:49.520
What's with you? We do this every day, man.

445
00:28:51.080 --> 00:28:53.960
What did you do before this?

446
00:28:58.640 --> 00:28:59.640
Are you curious?

447
00:29:11.640 --> 00:29:15.280
I used to be a track athlete.

448
00:29:15.680 --> 00:29:16.720
Wanna know something?

449
00:29:17.960 --> 00:29:22.040
I won't be scared when
I draw a dot on my face.

450
00:29:26.160 --> 00:29:28.160
Then why'd you quit?

451
00:29:28.880 --> 00:29:31.520
I didn't quit, I got cut.

452
00:29:33.240 --> 00:29:35.680
Because I wore thick
makeup during a competition.

453
00:29:36.880 --> 00:29:40.280
Here, no one cares.

454
00:29:42.800 --> 00:29:45.360
Hey, why are you blushing?

455
00:29:45.440 --> 00:29:48.480
No, I'm not.
You are now.

456
00:29:48.560 --> 00:29:49.920
No way.
You excited?

457
00:29:50.000 --> 00:29:51.600
You know I'm married.

458
00:29:51.640 --> 00:29:52.640
Then get divorced.

459
00:29:52.680 --> 00:29:55.800
Stop messing around. It's offensive.

460
00:29:55.840 --> 00:29:58.000
How could you say that?

461
00:29:58.040 --> 00:29:59.120
Just tell me.
Stop it.

462
00:29:59.200 --> 00:30:02.000
I'm just hot.
Then take it off.

463
00:30:04.760 --> 00:30:07.440
Watch it, Jackie had
a hard time getting this.

464
00:30:08.040 --> 00:30:09.800
Okay.
That flash's from the Soviets.

465
00:30:10.120 --> 00:30:11.600
It's the only one in Korea.

466
00:30:14.200 --> 00:30:17.360
Waiting for the rain, how romantic.

467
00:30:17.400 --> 00:30:19.880
Good for you.

468
00:30:20.160 --> 00:30:22.800
If I wasn't so romantic,
I'd have died in Vietnam.

469
00:30:23.000 --> 00:30:24.720
There you go again.

470
00:30:25.360 --> 00:30:28.000
It rained for months during the monsoon.

471
00:30:32.680 --> 00:30:34.480
It sounded like ho of beats.

472
00:30:36.000 --> 00:30:37.840
The rain was so scary.

473
00:30:39.200 --> 00:30:41.400
I couldn't look out the
window at the hospital.

474
00:30:41.560 --> 00:30:43.320
Why do you remember that?

475
00:30:47.080 --> 00:30:50.480
Even hell is pleasant when you're young.

476
00:30:53.160 --> 00:30:54.160
Target on the move.

477
00:30:56.080 --> 00:30:58.640
Thought there was a
50% chance of rain today.

478
00:31:00.280 --> 00:31:02.000
Half-and-half, right?

479
00:31:02.320 --> 00:31:03.320
Disengage.

480
00:31:05.160 --> 00:31:08.080
The prosecution is putting off
filing charges on Joo Young.

481
00:31:08.120 --> 00:31:10.880
Politicians are asking whether
the case is being neglected.

482
00:31:10.920 --> 00:31:13.680
Since she holds a high position...

483
00:31:13.760 --> 00:31:17.960
Politicians and the press are waiting
for Mr. Joo's official statement.

484
00:31:18.160 --> 00:31:19.680
Look at the headlines.

485
00:31:19.760 --> 00:31:23.200
Public opinion is shifting on the
matter of Joo's nomination.

486
00:31:23.440 --> 00:31:26.240
30% approve, 53% disapprove.

487
00:31:26.360 --> 00:31:27.960
There are more who disapprove.

488
00:31:28.240 --> 00:31:30.480
Something's hidden behind the facts.

489
00:31:31.920 --> 00:31:34.160
Don't look at the words or letters.

490
00:31:34.560 --> 00:31:36.080
We need to read between the lines.

491
00:31:36.160 --> 00:31:38.640
At what truth they're hiding.

492
00:31:39.160 --> 00:31:41.360
You all learned it in school.

493
00:31:42.120 --> 00:31:44.360
Looking for the hidden meaning.

494
00:31:45.520 --> 00:31:47.400
Things are getting messed up.

495
00:31:57.920 --> 00:32:02.200
Look at Young-il. He's so hot.
Look how tall he is.

496
00:32:02.240 --> 00:32:03.600
He's just my type.

497
00:32:04.920 --> 00:32:06.080
What the hell?

498
00:32:07.440 --> 00:32:11.200
I thought you liked me.

499
00:32:13.480 --> 00:32:15.080
You bastard.

500
00:32:20.560 --> 00:32:21.560
Disengage.

501
00:32:21.600 --> 00:32:24.680
A media outlet reported on an
international bank account

502
00:32:24.840 --> 00:32:27.800
said to belong to Ms. Joo.

503
00:32:28.000 --> 00:32:29.136
It was under her English name, Stacy,

504
00:32:29.160 --> 00:32:29.760
Disengage.

505
00:32:29.920 --> 00:32:34.000
which she used during her study abroad.

506
00:32:34.040 --> 00:32:35.120
Target on the move.

507
00:32:35.320 --> 00:32:36.320
Stand by.

508
00:32:42.200 --> 00:32:43.200
Disengage.

509
00:32:43.320 --> 00:32:47.760
The prosecution will soon announce if
they will summon Ms. Joo Young.

510
00:32:48.080 --> 00:32:50.360
Cloudy skies continue today.

511
00:32:50.480 --> 00:32:53.520
Rain is expected throughout the country.

512
00:32:53.600 --> 00:32:56.200
Please remember your umbrellas.

513
00:33:02.400 --> 00:33:03.400
Disengage.

514
00:33:12.560 --> 00:33:13.560
Stand by.

515
00:33:19.240 --> 00:33:20.520
Jeom-man, follow them!

516
00:33:20.840 --> 00:33:22.440
Now!

517
00:33:23.080 --> 00:33:25.120
Do you have a Swiss bank account?

518
00:33:25.440 --> 00:33:26.440
What are you doing?

519
00:33:37.240 --> 00:33:39.480
Ms. Joo's prosecution
announcement is delayed...

520
00:33:39.520 --> 00:33:40.600
Target on the move.

521
00:33:40.960 --> 00:33:41.960
Stand by.

522
00:33:43.800 --> 00:33:44.800
You excited?

523
00:33:49.800 --> 00:33:51.600
We'll go ahead with this much rain, right?

524
00:33:54.400 --> 00:33:55.400
Probably.

525
00:33:57.880 --> 00:33:59.440
I think it'll be okay today.

526
00:34:00.160 --> 00:34:01.800
What's okay?

527
00:34:02.960 --> 00:34:04.040
It's raining.

528
00:34:07.280 --> 00:34:08.280
Right.

529
00:34:10.880 --> 00:34:11.640
It's raining.

530
00:34:11.720 --> 00:34:14.320
Ms. Joo Young will be prosecuted.

531
00:34:14.600 --> 00:34:17.840
Today, the prosecution decided
to bring in Ms. Joo.

532
00:34:18.480 --> 00:34:21.480
If Mr. Joo does not speak for himself,

533
00:34:21.920 --> 00:34:24.320
his disapproval rates
will continue to increase.

534
00:34:24.400 --> 00:34:29.760
We surmise that the prosecution
has located a secret fund.

535
00:34:33.600 --> 00:34:34.880
This is Joo Sung-jik.

536
00:34:37.480 --> 00:34:39.280
I choose Joo Young.

537
00:34:39.840 --> 00:34:41.400
Take care of it right away.

538
00:34:44.840 --> 00:34:46.320
Choose Joo Young?

539
00:34:48.280 --> 00:34:51.960
Hey, can you do that for me?

540
00:35:00.880 --> 00:35:03.720
Don't like me too much. You'll get hurt.

541
00:35:04.400 --> 00:35:07.040
You always end up screwing things up.

542
00:35:08.240 --> 00:35:11.160
Didn't I sound like Young-il?
Shut up.

543
00:35:23.080 --> 00:35:24.160
Ms. Joo is prosecuted!

544
00:35:24.200 --> 00:35:26.360
Prosecuted... Ms. Joo is prosecuted!

545
00:35:33.120 --> 00:35:34.520
10 seconds. Stand by.

546
00:35:34.640 --> 00:35:35.640
Stand by.

547
00:35:35.760 --> 00:35:38.360
Bring up the headlines.

548
00:35:38.480 --> 00:35:40.240
Here we go. And cue!

549
00:35:40.320 --> 00:35:42.640
The prosecution is selecting a team,

550
00:35:42.680 --> 00:35:47.240
and the public is wondering about
Mr. Joo's next move.

551
00:35:56.720 --> 00:35:57.720
Your mother...

552
00:35:58.680 --> 00:36:00.840
I never thought she would do that.

553
00:36:01.520 --> 00:36:03.600
I was sure she didn't do it.

554
00:36:03.680 --> 00:36:04.680
So...

555
00:36:05.520 --> 00:36:08.600
I reported her to the prosecution myself
to clear the false rumors.

556
00:36:08.680 --> 00:36:12.480
That way, we clear our names.
I trusted your mother!

557
00:36:15.640 --> 00:36:16.840
Target on the move.

558
00:36:20.840 --> 00:36:22.600
They're here! Here they are!

559
00:36:24.040 --> 00:36:27.960
The prosecution decided to bring
in Ms. Joo. How do you feel?

560
00:36:28.040 --> 00:36:30.080
Tell us how you feel, Ms. Joo!

561
00:36:30.160 --> 00:36:32.160
Tell us your next steps!

562
00:36:32.280 --> 00:36:34.440
Ms. Joo! How do you feel?

563
00:36:34.800 --> 00:36:38.680
Hello, this is Joo Sung-jik.

564
00:36:38.720 --> 00:36:40.120
Stand by.

565
00:36:41.160 --> 00:36:42.480
Joo Sung-jik is making statement.

566
00:36:42.920 --> 00:36:49.160
As of today, I give up my candidacy
for Prosecutor General.

567
00:36:49.200 --> 00:36:52.400
Then do you recognize the
charges against Ms. Joo?

568
00:36:52.920 --> 00:36:54.640
Ms. Joo, a word please.

569
00:36:55.120 --> 00:36:56.960
Stand by.
Got it.

570
00:37:00.480 --> 00:37:01.480
Check.

571
00:37:02.280 --> 00:37:04.640
My personal issues have
raised concerns to many.

572
00:37:05.040 --> 00:37:06.040
Jackie?

573
00:37:07.960 --> 00:37:09.120
Jackie, come in.

574
00:37:12.880 --> 00:37:14.280
Wol-cheon, go check.

575
00:37:14.640 --> 00:37:21.040
Regardless of the truth,
I was wrong to upset the public.

576
00:37:27.720 --> 00:37:29.400
She's gone.
What?

577
00:37:29.480 --> 00:37:31.440
Many workers supported me,

578
00:37:31.640 --> 00:37:33.000
Shouldn't we stop?

579
00:37:33.160 --> 00:37:39.360
I thank you, and apologize to you all.

580
00:37:40.760 --> 00:37:42.600
I choose Joo Young.

581
00:37:43.200 --> 00:37:45.040
If the Sweepers move first...

582
00:37:46.600 --> 00:37:48.200
Joo Young could be hit first.

583
00:37:49.280 --> 00:37:50.560
Continue with the plan.

584
00:37:51.400 --> 00:37:53.600
Wol-cheon, take Jaekie's post.
Alright.

585
00:37:53.720 --> 00:37:55.120
Do you admit to the charges?

586
00:37:55.320 --> 00:37:57.840
Did you inherit your mother's slush fund?

587
00:37:57.920 --> 00:38:00.440
A word please, Ms. Joo!

588
00:38:00.520 --> 00:38:01.520
Please! Tell us!

589
00:38:01.600 --> 00:38:02.600
Say something!

590
00:38:02.680 --> 00:38:04.520
What will happen next?

591
00:38:19.280 --> 00:38:20.280
Right now!

592
00:39:23.080 --> 00:39:24.080
Joo Sung-jik...

593
00:40:07.160 --> 00:40:08.400
Prepare a headline!

594
00:40:08.480 --> 00:40:10.400
Joo Sung-jik, accident after speech.

595
00:40:11.680 --> 00:40:13.240
Camera 1, closer!

596
00:40:13.600 --> 00:40:14.600
Close-up!

597
00:40:14.640 --> 00:40:16.240
Camera 2, come in!

598
00:40:26.400 --> 00:40:27.040
Hey, Joo Young!

599
00:40:27.160 --> 00:40:29.920
Flip her over!
Hold her!

600
00:40:36.200 --> 00:40:37.280
Go find Jackie.

601
00:40:37.360 --> 00:40:38.720
I'll take the car.

602
00:40:39.000 --> 00:40:40.000
And Jeom-man?

603
00:40:57.840 --> 00:41:01.120
She's not on the streets. I'll look again.

604
00:41:02.080 --> 00:41:03.440
I'll check the alleys.

605
00:41:04.360 --> 00:41:05.360
Keep looking.

606
00:41:14.160 --> 00:41:15.160
I saw Jackie.

607
00:41:15.240 --> 00:41:16.240
Where?

608
00:41:16.600 --> 00:41:18.040
By the bus station.

609
00:41:18.560 --> 00:41:19.680
I'll go.

610
00:41:20.760 --> 00:41:22.040
Jeom-man, come this way.

611
00:41:23.040 --> 00:41:24.400
Okay, I will.

612
00:42:39.840 --> 00:42:41.000
What happened?

613
00:42:41.840 --> 00:42:42.840
Young-il.

614
00:42:43.640 --> 00:42:46.160
What was that sound? Can you hear me?

615
00:43:05.200 --> 00:43:06.720
This is an accident, right?

616
00:43:10.480 --> 00:43:13.560
I'm... alright.

617
00:43:15.600 --> 00:43:17.440
No problem.

618
00:44:36.280 --> 00:44:37.440
Are you alright?

619
00:44:42.960 --> 00:44:44.040
Who were you calling?

620
00:44:45.480 --> 00:44:46.760
Jackie.

621
00:44:47.120 --> 00:44:48.320
I can't reach her.

622
00:44:49.760 --> 00:44:50.760
Where's Jeom-man?

623
00:45:20.480 --> 00:45:21.920
This is Jeom-man's.

624
00:45:27.520 --> 00:45:30.840
No, it can't be.

625
00:45:31.840 --> 00:45:33.000
It's not true, right?

626
00:45:33.920 --> 00:45:34.920
Right?

627
00:45:37.560 --> 00:45:39.440
Did he really die?

628
00:45:42.840 --> 00:45:44.360
Say something!

629
00:46:07.600 --> 00:46:09.200
Was it really an accident?

630
00:46:09.800 --> 00:46:11.520
The case with Ms. Lee, too.

631
00:46:13.160 --> 00:46:16.960
This is the Sweepers, right?

632
00:46:19.400 --> 00:46:21.560
I saw someone right before it happened.

633
00:46:23.080 --> 00:46:24.080
Where?

634
00:46:27.240 --> 00:46:29.480
There was someone at the bus station.

635
00:46:30.240 --> 00:46:31.920
Did you see who it was?

636
00:46:35.320 --> 00:46:36.560
They disappeared.

637
00:46:41.320 --> 00:46:43.760
Let's think.

638
00:46:44.600 --> 00:46:47.200
There might be more than one person.

639
00:46:47.800 --> 00:46:50.000
They were after me.

640
00:46:51.120 --> 00:46:52.160
One person.

641
00:46:53.720 --> 00:46:54.720
Two people.

642
00:46:55.360 --> 00:46:56.720
I saw Jackie.

643
00:46:56.960 --> 00:46:57.960
Three people.

644
00:46:59.120 --> 00:47:00.880
By the bus station.

645
00:47:01.840 --> 00:47:04.240
Wol-cheon led me to the site.

646
00:47:05.800 --> 00:47:07.600
Jackie's been weird lately.

647
00:47:08.480 --> 00:47:09.960
This was in the car.

648
00:47:11.200 --> 00:47:13.280
She hasn't been
answering the walkie-talkie.

649
00:47:14.560 --> 00:47:16.360
Isn't it weird?

650
00:47:16.800 --> 00:47:19.000
Are you suspecting Jackie?

651
00:47:27.240 --> 00:47:28.840
I don't know.

652
00:47:32.360 --> 00:47:33.360
It can't be.

653
00:47:39.200 --> 00:47:40.960
Did Sung-jik ask for this?

654
00:47:43.720 --> 00:47:45.480
No, it wasn't done by him.

655
00:47:47.000 --> 00:47:49.320
With his death, her wrongdoing is gone.

656
00:47:49.760 --> 00:47:55.480
Ms. Joo is suspected of inheriting
her mother's slush fund.

657
00:47:55.680 --> 00:47:57.640
And her mother's money became hers.

658
00:47:59.920 --> 00:48:00.920
It's Joo Young.

659
00:48:01.800 --> 00:48:04.720
Young-il, if we're being wiretapped,

660
00:48:04.960 --> 00:48:07.160
someone's selling our intel
from the inside, right?

661
00:48:09.680 --> 00:48:11.320
That's the only possibility.

662
00:48:14.840 --> 00:48:16.520
We can't trust anyone now.

663
00:48:22.120 --> 00:48:24.000
That's the world we made.

664
00:48:24.760 --> 00:48:26.480
I can't trust anyone.

665
00:48:28.320 --> 00:48:29.880
Are we in danger too?

666
00:48:30.840 --> 00:48:31.920
The only one of us...

667
00:48:32.520 --> 00:48:34.000
I'm done here.

668
00:48:34.160 --> 00:48:39.360
who could talk to Young is Wol-cheon.

669
00:48:47.400 --> 00:48:48.960
Let's hide for now.

670
00:48:53.120 --> 00:48:54.280
If you want...

671
00:48:57.360 --> 00:48:58.920
you can stay at my place.

672
00:48:59.160 --> 00:49:00.680
It's safer to stay apart.

673
00:49:03.440 --> 00:49:06.680
Yes, that'll be better.

674
00:49:07.120 --> 00:49:08.400
How long?

675
00:49:09.400 --> 00:49:10.600
I'll call you.

676
00:49:18.960 --> 00:49:22.200
I got 10,000 more subscribers today.

677
00:49:22.720 --> 00:49:25.360
Thanks to you, I can now get donations.

678
00:49:25.520 --> 00:49:26.520
Thank you.

679
00:49:26.880 --> 00:49:28.520
Now, Joo Sung-jik is dead.

680
00:49:28.720 --> 00:49:33.480
Breaking news. Mr. Joo
Sung-jik passed away today.

681
00:49:33.800 --> 00:49:38.160
The cause is electrical shock
from broadcasting equipment.

682
00:49:38.200 --> 00:49:41.520
Joo's daughter, meanwhile,
is hospitalized from shock.

683
00:49:41.760 --> 00:49:45.880
She has epilepsy, which may be the reason.

684
00:49:46.440 --> 00:49:49.880
Epilepsy? That's all a show.

685
00:49:50.880 --> 00:49:55.280
The media knows the
truth, but it hides it. Why?

686
00:49:56.040 --> 00:49:57.960
The media is a business.

687
00:49:58.720 --> 00:50:00.720
It's a distribution industry.

688
00:50:01.000 --> 00:50:04.960
You consume, the press distributes.
Then who produces?

689
00:50:05.240 --> 00:50:10.000
Think smart. Producing death
is a high value business.

690
00:50:10.160 --> 00:50:13.120
Political power might shift,
and businesses might go down.

691
00:50:13.360 --> 00:50:16.800
A personal media post showed
Ms. Joo's old classmate.

692
00:50:16.880 --> 00:50:21.000
She was called Spasm
Joo. Because of her seizures.

693
00:50:21.360 --> 00:50:23.760
I can only do business
by selling truth to you.

694
00:50:24.360 --> 00:50:27.840
There is only one truth.

695
00:50:38.280 --> 00:50:42.560
Hello, I'm Inspector Yang,
here to inspect the accident.

696
00:50:43.320 --> 00:50:46.200
I'm sorry for your loss.

697
00:50:46.960 --> 00:50:52.360
Have you ever seen this man?

698
00:51:00.920 --> 00:51:01.920
No.

699
00:51:04.080 --> 00:51:05.920
He may seem like a reporter,

700
00:51:06.000 --> 00:51:11.760
but he died in a bus accident right
after your father's death.

701
00:51:12.240 --> 00:51:15.880
Um Jae-man, 21 years old.
He was a criminal, from juvy.

702
00:51:16.000 --> 00:51:20.080
He has a child, but his wife doesn't
even know why he was there.

703
00:51:20.360 --> 00:51:24.000
You think the bus accident is related
to my father's accident?

704
00:51:26.760 --> 00:51:30.800
Your father had life insurance.

705
00:51:31.120 --> 00:51:35.000
5 policies, totalling $1.5
million. Did you know?

706
00:51:37.200 --> 00:51:38.200
No.

707
00:51:38.680 --> 00:51:42.560
He changed the recipient to you
a couple days before he died.

708
00:51:43.280 --> 00:51:45.760
Do you think this wasn't an accident?

709
00:51:47.120 --> 00:51:50.040
Of course not. It was
obviously an accident.

710
00:51:50.240 --> 00:51:52.480
There's so much news footage.

711
00:51:56.160 --> 00:51:57.480
You call that evidence?

712
00:52:00.320 --> 00:52:01.000
What?

713
00:52:01.320 --> 00:52:03.360
What do you think of the
people who took them?

714
00:52:03.600 --> 00:52:06.400
They're uploading videos like crazy.

715
00:52:08.120 --> 00:52:10.400
Guess you don't think
reporters are the problem?

716
00:52:12.400 --> 00:52:13.840
You're here to see me,

717
00:52:15.240 --> 00:52:16.640
and you talk about insurance money?

718
00:52:19.680 --> 00:52:23.600
Go tell the reporters. They'll like that.

719
00:52:23.840 --> 00:52:25.440
Alright, calm down.

720
00:52:26.000 --> 00:52:29.120
We're looking into their
excessive actions too.

721
00:52:31.680 --> 00:52:34.760
Then you should've
gone to the reporters first.

722
00:52:39.720 --> 00:52:43.720
I admired Mr. Joo too.

723
00:52:45.800 --> 00:52:48.200
Now, I'll get going.

724
00:53:01.800 --> 00:53:04.960
I just saw her.

725
00:53:05.200 --> 00:53:06.480
She's interesting.

726
00:53:07.960 --> 00:53:12.600
It'll take about an
hour. You can't join me.

727
00:53:12.680 --> 00:53:17.000
Before I arrive, list all reporters
who were at the accident.

728
00:53:21.360 --> 00:53:23.480
Jackie's been weird lately.

729
00:53:26.760 --> 00:53:28.880
She hasn't been
answering the walkie-talkie.

730
00:53:30.040 --> 00:53:32.160
Isn't it weird?

731
00:53:55.640 --> 00:53:56.760
Odd Eye.

732
00:54:22.000 --> 00:54:23.480
Mommy's home.

733
00:54:23.680 --> 00:54:29.480
How adorable.

734
00:54:30.080 --> 00:54:33.400
How are you?

735
00:54:34.400 --> 00:54:37.040
Odd Eye, the house is a mess, right?

736
00:54:42.280 --> 00:54:44.480
Wait here.

737
00:55:01.360 --> 00:55:02.560
How long has it been?

738
00:55:04.280 --> 00:55:06.040
About a year?

739
00:55:07.800 --> 00:55:10.720
My brain's ruined because of the morphine.

740
00:55:12.640 --> 00:55:13.840
I'm not sick.

741
00:55:14.040 --> 00:55:16.760
Nothing's wrong. I'm fine.

742
00:55:19.560 --> 00:55:21.640
Really, I'm not sick.

743
00:55:25.200 --> 00:55:28.600
I promised you I'd stop.

744
00:55:34.040 --> 00:55:37.560
I would've died if it weren't for you.

745
00:55:47.880 --> 00:55:49.160
What's your diagnosis?

746
00:55:52.880 --> 00:55:55.120
Alz...

747
00:55:58.600 --> 00:56:00.040
Alzheimer's.

748
00:56:02.840 --> 00:56:03.920
You know,

749
00:56:05.360 --> 00:56:07.360
you can't trust the doctor.

750
00:56:10.760 --> 00:56:11.840
What happened?

751
00:56:14.240 --> 00:56:19.480
You used to be so chatty,
but now you're quiet.

752
00:56:19.760 --> 00:56:21.360
You're like Young-il.

753
00:56:22.880 --> 00:56:25.280
Odd Eye only talked a
lot when he was nervous.

754
00:56:25.480 --> 00:56:30.880
Right. He talked a lot
while we set up a plot.

755
00:56:31.760 --> 00:56:33.520
You were scared, right?

756
00:56:37.440 --> 00:56:38.600
Oh right.

757
00:56:40.280 --> 00:56:43.320
It was raining, right?

758
00:56:44.160 --> 00:56:45.840
I was waiting for that.

759
00:56:47.920 --> 00:56:49.360
You were there too.

760
00:56:50.440 --> 00:56:51.960
You saw Odd Eye?

761
00:56:52.400 --> 00:56:56.360
Yeah, you were across the street.

762
00:56:57.040 --> 00:57:01.200
But you were so fast, I lost you.

763
00:57:01.880 --> 00:57:04.600
I've been looking for you.

764
00:57:07.360 --> 00:57:12.240
But why'd you come
back? You shouldn't have.

765
00:57:13.120 --> 00:57:14.920
Why do you think I left?

766
00:57:15.120 --> 00:57:17.440
You said you wanted a normal life.

767
00:57:17.920 --> 00:57:19.880
I want to live a normal life.

768
00:57:21.240 --> 00:57:22.800
You understand, right?

769
00:57:23.080 --> 00:57:25.080
Do you think it's safe to leave here?

770
00:57:28.000 --> 00:57:31.920
I found a wiretap in our office.

771
00:57:38.360 --> 00:57:39.920
What do you mean?

772
00:57:44.200 --> 00:57:45.720
Odd Eye is dead.

773
00:57:46.160 --> 00:57:49.280
What are you saying? You told me.

774
00:57:49.880 --> 00:57:51.840
You wanted to quit.

775
00:57:53.800 --> 00:57:55.520
I said, Odd Eye is dead.

776
00:57:55.720 --> 00:57:58.600
It's because of Young-il, isn't it?

777
00:58:02.480 --> 00:58:05.000
The Sweepers killed Odd Eye!

778
00:58:06.720 --> 00:58:08.520
You're scaring me, Odd Eye.

779
00:58:32.600 --> 00:58:35.800
Mr. Joo had $1.5 million in life insurance!

780
00:58:35.840 --> 00:58:38.240
This is a double deal.

781
00:58:38.440 --> 00:58:39.280
She's an ambitious one.

782
00:58:39.360 --> 00:58:42.280
That money will go to
his daughter, Joo Young.

783
00:58:42.400 --> 00:58:44.080
Why did Sung-jik die?

784
00:58:45.320 --> 00:58:46.560
That's not important.

785
00:58:47.040 --> 00:58:48.920
He was going to die anyway.

786
00:58:49.360 --> 00:58:52.320
His daughter benefited the most? Nope.

787
00:58:52.400 --> 00:58:54.600
Hauser TV predicted Sung-jik's death!

788
00:58:54.680 --> 00:58:55.600
He's on a roll.

789
00:58:55.680 --> 00:58:57.160
He has a new prediction!

790
00:58:57.240 --> 00:58:59.536
You know the bus accident that
happened after Mr. Joo's death?

791
00:58:59.560 --> 00:59:01.440
Was that really a coincidence?

792
00:59:01.720 --> 00:59:05.520
There was an accomplice at the crime site.

793
00:59:11.160 --> 00:59:15.520
Mothman was there when
Mr. Joo died. Look carefully.

794
00:59:15.840 --> 00:59:17.880
I know who it is. Aren't you curious?

795
00:59:18.320 --> 00:59:23.040
I won't be suicided! Don't forget.

796
00:59:29.840 --> 00:59:30.840
Yes.

797
00:59:32.080 --> 00:59:34.360
I heard about my father's insurance money.

798
00:59:35.840 --> 00:59:37.960
The reporters must've found out,

799
00:59:39.080 --> 00:59:41.040
so we need to move fast.

800
00:59:41.880 --> 00:59:44.800
Yes, let's talk tomorrow.

801
00:59:49.120 --> 00:59:52.120
Ms. Joo Young! Look here!

802
00:59:52.400 --> 00:59:54.680
How do you feel about your father's death?

803
00:59:55.040 --> 00:59:57.760
Ms. Joo, a word please!

804
00:59:58.200 --> 00:59:59.840
Back off!

805
01:00:28.040 --> 01:00:30.280
Oh, hello. Sit down, please.

806
01:00:48.120 --> 01:00:50.240
Joo Young refused the documents.

807
01:00:52.200 --> 01:00:54.080
Is it not over yet?

808
01:01:17.080 --> 01:01:21.200
Meanwhile at 1 p.m. today there
was a tower crane accident.

809
01:01:21.560 --> 01:01:23.360
Also, there were additional deaths.

810
01:01:23.400 --> 01:01:25.960
Could it be the Sweepers?

811
01:02:14.840 --> 01:02:16.240
Who's Mothman?

812
01:02:16.320 --> 01:02:19.000
I believe he's a man in his mid-30s,
with short hair, slender build,

813
01:02:19.040 --> 01:02:20.800
and about 6 feet tall.

814
01:02:20.880 --> 01:02:21.880
Yes, hello.

815
01:02:21.960 --> 01:02:23.120
He must have a great mask.

816
01:02:23.160 --> 01:02:25.000
You must smile well to hide your identity.

817
01:02:25.160 --> 01:02:26.840
Yes, I did get a call.

818
01:02:27.880 --> 01:02:29.696
I can't cause any
inconvenience to the solicitor.

819
01:02:29.720 --> 01:02:31.560
Mothman must be affiliated with a company.

820
01:02:31.600 --> 01:02:34.320
Someplace related to accidents,
such as insurance companies.

821
01:02:35.320 --> 01:02:38.800
And he must have connections
with police and high-ranking officials.

822
01:02:38.920 --> 01:02:41.280
Sirs, Hauser made a new prophecy.

823
01:02:41.480 --> 01:02:44.840
He said that Mothman killed Joo Sung-jik.

824
01:02:44.960 --> 01:02:49.320
This Mothman guy killed Joo,
at the daughter's request.

825
01:02:49.360 --> 01:02:51.280
And he only works with the big shots.

826
01:02:51.520 --> 01:02:53.400
It's not an individual.

827
01:02:53.600 --> 01:02:55.520
It must be an organization.

828
01:02:55.600 --> 01:02:58.280
Related to some corporation
or the government...

829
01:02:58.320 --> 01:03:00.560
How'd he get this info?

830
01:03:01.520 --> 01:03:03.000
He said he has photos as proof.

831
01:03:03.160 --> 01:03:07.720
Plus, he predicted there
will be another accident.

832
01:03:07.800 --> 01:03:10.040
People related to Joo Sung-jik,

833
01:03:10.160 --> 01:03:13.640
or journalists are the next targets.

834
01:03:13.760 --> 01:03:17.200
People will keep dying, everyone.

835
01:03:17.640 --> 01:03:22.720
People around Joo, and connected
journalists will die in accidents.

836
01:03:22.800 --> 01:03:23.800
Wait and see.

837
01:03:24.600 --> 01:03:26.360
My words will hit the mark again.

838
01:03:36.440 --> 01:03:38.560
He's probably not alone. Why?

839
01:03:38.600 --> 01:03:41.280
Because killing Joo
Sung-jik isn't an easy job.

840
01:03:41.480 --> 01:03:43.680
There must be a team of two or more.

841
01:03:44.000 --> 01:03:46.800
Their age group will range
from middle age to youth.

842
01:03:46.920 --> 01:03:48.840
So that they can fit in anywhere.

843
01:03:49.480 --> 01:03:52.520
They are hiding among us, perfectly.

844
01:03:59.320 --> 01:04:00.520
They must be his team members.

845
01:04:32.800 --> 01:04:34.120
The day Joo Sung-jik died.

846
01:04:50.120 --> 01:04:51.120
Seo Hee-won.

847
01:04:55.520 --> 01:04:56.640
Newsroom reporter.

848
01:04:59.920 --> 01:05:01.200
She's the next target.

849
01:05:07.920 --> 01:05:09.000
Lee Chi-hyun.

850
01:05:11.400 --> 01:05:12.480
He's a Sweeper.

851
01:05:13.680 --> 01:05:15.560
You still haven't found the insured?

852
01:05:17.680 --> 01:05:18.680
And the solicitor?

853
01:05:19.800 --> 01:05:21.520
Didn't you meet that old lady?

854
01:05:22.160 --> 01:05:25.600
The insured is the target,
and the solicitor is the client.

855
01:05:25.880 --> 01:05:28.080
Okay, just send me the documents then.

856
01:05:28.400 --> 01:05:29.040
Yes.

857
01:05:29.160 --> 01:05:30.880
And... Hello?

858
01:05:32.000 --> 01:05:33.000
Excuse me.

859
01:05:33.200 --> 01:05:35.760
I'm Inspector Yang from the
accident investigation team.

860
01:05:37.920 --> 01:05:39.720
You're a cop, and you still work like this?

861
01:05:39.800 --> 01:05:40.360
Sorry?

862
01:05:40.800 --> 01:05:41.960
We've never met?

863
01:05:42.240 --> 01:05:43.240
Right.

864
01:05:43.320 --> 01:05:46.920
I told you, you need a warrant
if you want documents.

865
01:05:47.040 --> 01:05:50.000
Yes, I understand.

866
01:05:50.520 --> 01:05:52.960
I'm just going to ask one question.

867
01:05:54.160 --> 01:05:56.320
Do you know why Mr. Joo took out insurance?

868
01:05:56.800 --> 01:05:58.720
5 policies seems excessive, doesn't it?

869
01:05:59.120 --> 01:06:02.560
I heard he applied for them
after his wife passed away.

870
01:06:03.680 --> 01:06:06.840
That's the way he handles things.
He prepares in advance.

871
01:06:07.840 --> 01:06:11.280
You get a lot of calls
from the media about Joo?

872
01:06:11.600 --> 01:06:13.960
Yes, and I'm handling it well.

873
01:06:14.040 --> 01:06:15.600
They all know better.

874
01:06:16.040 --> 01:06:19.600
And I have nothing to say publicly.

875
01:06:19.800 --> 01:06:23.360
Then can you talk to me privately?

876
01:06:23.480 --> 01:06:27.440
You need a search warrant
if you want me to talk.

877
01:06:30.120 --> 01:06:32.600
This is all I have about Mr. Joo.

878
01:06:32.640 --> 01:06:34.240
The details are erased.

879
01:06:41.040 --> 01:06:41.880
Thank you.

880
01:06:41.960 --> 01:06:43.080
No problem.

881
01:06:44.280 --> 01:06:45.640
See you again.
Sure.

882
01:06:47.040 --> 01:06:48.080
A cop was here.

883
01:06:48.520 --> 01:06:49.520
Yeah.

884
01:06:50.240 --> 01:06:53.640
All officers are the
same, annoying as hell.

885
01:06:54.080 --> 01:06:56.960
She thinks of us as just
another insurance company.

886
01:06:57.160 --> 01:06:59.840
Our clients won't put up with any of this.

887
01:07:01.080 --> 01:07:03.320
Take care of the
Seongsu case as I told you.

888
01:07:03.400 --> 01:07:05.040
Don't worry about the press.

889
01:07:05.600 --> 01:07:08.600
The good news is the
insured finally passed away.

890
01:07:09.680 --> 01:07:12.360
We just need to end things our own way.

891
01:07:13.440 --> 01:07:15.760
Alright, see you at the office sometime.

892
01:07:49.360 --> 01:07:50.840
Problem one is solved.

893
01:07:51.080 --> 01:07:52.400
Breaking news.

894
01:07:53.120 --> 01:07:55.120
My channel will get blown up soon.

895
01:07:56.040 --> 01:07:59.040
As you all expected,
they started slandering me.

896
01:08:00.320 --> 01:08:03.520
But I won't go down like this.

897
01:08:04.360 --> 01:08:09.200
Is it really that hard to find an old lady
and an insured who ran away?

898
01:08:14.360 --> 01:08:17.880
I told you, that old lady fell from
the building and got hurt. Yes.

899
01:08:19.080 --> 01:08:22.120
Once we get in touch,
let's find the insured and wrap this up.

900
01:08:22.200 --> 01:08:24.440
If not, other investigators
will start their move.

901
01:08:30.800 --> 01:08:32.480
These are the final documents.

902
01:08:34.080 --> 01:08:37.280
I took steps so the press
won't bother you anymore.

903
01:08:48.520 --> 01:08:50.080
No need to see you anymore.

904
01:08:50.400 --> 01:08:51.840
Call me any time.

905
01:08:53.000 --> 01:08:56.760
My door is always open to VIPs like you.

906
01:09:53.480 --> 01:09:54.480
Young-il?

907
01:09:54.880 --> 01:09:56.480
Why are you there?

908
01:09:59.720 --> 01:10:02.560
I just got the money from Joo Young.

909
01:10:02.640 --> 01:10:04.680
You mean from the Sweepers, not her.

910
01:10:06.360 --> 01:10:08.960
You're taking this wrong.
I couldn't reach you.

911
01:10:09.440 --> 01:10:11.120
Something urgent came up.

912
01:10:11.480 --> 01:10:13.080
You know my situation is urgent.

913
01:10:13.280 --> 01:10:15.360
Then why did you come
to the Sweepers' office?

914
01:10:16.560 --> 01:10:17.600
Did you find them?

915
01:10:17.680 --> 01:10:18.840
Don't pretend you don't know.

916
01:10:18.920 --> 01:10:21.480
You know better than this.
Why should I betray you?

917
01:10:21.760 --> 01:10:23.880
When did you start contacting Lee Chi-hyun?

918
01:10:24.200 --> 01:10:27.160
You're getting this all wrong.
Let's meet and talk about it, okay?

919
01:10:27.640 --> 01:10:30.320
Is that why you killed Jeom-man?

920
01:10:31.200 --> 01:10:32.880
You think I killed him?

921
01:10:34.200 --> 01:10:36.600
Listen to me.

922
01:10:42.120 --> 01:10:43.400
You are here, right?

923
01:10:45.800 --> 01:10:47.680
I'll explain everything. Let's meet first.

924
01:10:47.760 --> 01:10:49.400
You told me that you saw Jackie.

925
01:10:50.320 --> 01:10:52.280
You're the one who
lured me to the accident.

926
01:10:53.240 --> 01:10:54.840
I really saw Jackie!

927
01:10:55.040 --> 01:10:56.360
Prove it.

928
01:10:58.240 --> 01:11:01.200
I said we should stop when Jackie
went missing, you heard me.

929
01:11:01.240 --> 01:11:05.480
You knew I wouldn't stop.

930
01:11:18.360 --> 01:11:19.920
I don't know about the others...

931
01:11:22.920 --> 01:11:24.960
but I thought you trusted me.

932
01:11:26.000 --> 01:11:27.960
Is that why you tried to kill me?

933
01:11:48.280 --> 01:11:49.920
Did you set this car up?

934
01:11:56.320 --> 01:11:57.880
Take the money and leave.

935
01:11:59.480 --> 01:12:00.720
Unless you want to die.

936
01:12:02.600 --> 01:12:04.960
Are you that curious about the Sweepers?

937
01:12:08.600 --> 01:12:10.040
You are, aren't you?

938
01:12:11.400 --> 01:12:13.560
I finally understand why Odd Eye died.

939
01:12:13.960 --> 01:12:16.360
You make people insane, you know that?

940
01:12:16.800 --> 01:12:17.600
Shut up.

941
01:12:17.720 --> 01:12:20.120
He didn't trust you, he was scared of you.

942
01:12:20.200 --> 01:12:21.280
You still don't get it?

943
01:12:21.400 --> 01:12:22.000
Shut up!

944
01:12:22.040 --> 01:12:23.360
You don't trust anyone.

945
01:12:23.560 --> 01:12:25.600
You don't even try to. Am I wrong?

946
01:12:25.800 --> 01:12:27.240
I pity Odd Eye so bad.

947
01:12:27.360 --> 01:12:29.560
He wouldn't have died like that
if he hadn't met you!

948
01:12:29.640 --> 01:12:30.760
Shut up!

949
01:12:58.800 --> 01:13:01.080
Underground parking lot, right?
Yes, hurry.

950
01:13:01.280 --> 01:13:02.280
Yes, sir.

951
01:13:02.480 --> 01:13:05.120
Yes, I'm waiting at the
back door parking lot.

952
01:13:05.200 --> 01:13:07.160
Yes, I'll take pictures if I see something.

953
01:13:17.680 --> 01:13:19.280
Someone fell.

954
01:13:21.200 --> 01:13:22.800
What's that? It's Joo Young!

955
01:13:24.880 --> 01:13:26.200
Joo Young killed herself!

956
01:13:26.280 --> 01:13:27.960
She's dead!

957
01:13:28.840 --> 01:13:30.400
Joo Young fell!

958
01:13:31.440 --> 01:13:32.840
This should be breaking news!

959
01:13:33.160 --> 01:13:35.800
Bring everyone here. This is a scoop!

960
01:13:40.960 --> 01:13:45.480
Odd Eye, help me. I think
somebody came for me.

961
01:13:50.600 --> 01:13:52.760
Hold on! Get out of the way.

962
01:13:53.680 --> 01:13:55.040
Yes, all confirmed.

963
01:13:55.920 --> 01:13:57.560
Back off.

964
01:13:58.960 --> 01:14:00.520
You can't take pictures.

965
01:14:02.360 --> 01:14:03.240
Is she conscious?

966
01:14:03.360 --> 01:14:04.440
No.

967
01:14:04.640 --> 01:14:05.720
We'll transport her.

968
01:14:18.440 --> 01:14:21.000
I told you, that old lady
fell from the building.

969
01:14:21.120 --> 01:14:22.120
Yes.

970
01:14:22.800 --> 01:14:26.120
Once we make contact, let's find
the insured and wrap this case up.

971
01:14:26.160 --> 01:14:28.400
If not, other investigators
will start to move.

972
01:14:43.480 --> 01:14:44.640
I'm next.

973
01:14:55.760 --> 01:14:58.120
Yes, we wrapped up the basic investigation.

974
01:14:58.200 --> 01:14:59.000
Yes.

975
01:14:59.120 --> 01:15:00.216
I'll call you if I need anything.

976
01:15:00.240 --> 01:15:00.680
Alright.

977
01:15:00.800 --> 01:15:02.640
Why can't people live straight?

978
01:15:02.680 --> 01:15:03.960
They have no shame.

979
01:15:06.120 --> 01:15:09.280
Room 1002. The place next door got robbed.

980
01:15:11.480 --> 01:15:12.600
Excuse me.

981
01:15:13.920 --> 01:15:16.160
I just need to check something.

982
01:15:18.120 --> 01:15:19.160
Go on.

983
01:15:19.280 --> 01:15:21.920
Your neighbor got robbed,
but I can't specify the time.

984
01:15:22.360 --> 01:15:25.320
Did you hear any loud noise
yesterday by any chance?

985
01:15:26.160 --> 01:15:28.920
I just came, so I don't know.

986
01:15:31.920 --> 01:15:33.960
Let me check your ID.

987
01:15:43.480 --> 01:15:46.080
Run a check on him. Yoon Young-soo.

988
01:15:46.640 --> 01:15:51.080
870712-10382651. Yes.

989
01:15:52.320 --> 01:15:54.520
Mr. Yoon, what do you do for a living?

990
01:15:54.960 --> 01:15:56.680
I work for a security agency.

991
01:15:56.960 --> 01:15:58.440
A security agency?

992
01:16:02.320 --> 01:16:04.560
Did you hurt your hand at work?

993
01:16:06.240 --> 01:16:07.240
Yes.

994
01:16:07.760 --> 01:16:10.720
All right.

995
01:16:14.600 --> 01:16:17.080
There's been a rash of thefts these days.

996
01:16:51.760 --> 01:16:52.800
It's gone.

997
01:16:54.880 --> 01:16:56.480
The chess piece is gone.

998
01:17:17.560 --> 01:17:22.040
There really was a wiretap.

999
01:17:23.080 --> 01:17:25.280
If our home was exposed,

1000
01:17:26.840 --> 01:17:28.520
doesn't it mean we're done?

1001
01:17:29.520 --> 01:17:30.800
We will die.

1002
01:17:31.320 --> 01:17:32.720
We will Die...

1003
01:17:33.720 --> 01:17:39.120
Police have found a suicide note
in Joo Young's office.

1004
01:17:39.480 --> 01:17:42.840
Joo Young, the object of numerous rumors,

1005
01:17:42.920 --> 01:17:45.760
seems to have made a tragic choice.

1006
01:18:20.920 --> 01:18:23.560
Hello, this is Hauser.

1007
01:18:23.800 --> 01:18:25.480
I'll start the live broadcast.

1008
01:18:27.080 --> 01:18:29.600
Today will be a glorious day for Hauser TV.

1009
01:18:29.680 --> 01:18:32.920
Every media outlet in
this country will know me.

1010
01:18:33.040 --> 01:18:34.040
Why?

1011
01:18:34.840 --> 01:18:37.320
Something huge is about to happen!

1012
01:18:59.960 --> 01:19:00.960
Hello?

1013
01:19:01.840 --> 01:19:04.480
Yes, have you found the insured?

1014
01:19:06.200 --> 01:19:07.520
Are you sure you found him?

1015
01:19:08.440 --> 01:19:09.720
That's great.

1016
01:19:10.400 --> 01:19:13.080
I'm in a meeting, so call me later.

1017
01:19:13.120 --> 01:19:14.800
Got it. Yes.

1018
01:20:04.240 --> 01:20:06.800
The following news is about Joo Young

1019
01:20:06.880 --> 01:20:10.400
who made a large donation in
Mr. Joo's name before her passing...

1020
01:20:11.520 --> 01:20:12.800
Mothman, are you watching me?

1021
01:20:13.120 --> 01:20:14.200
I told you,

1022
01:20:14.480 --> 01:20:16.120
on the day Joo Sung-jik died,

1023
01:20:16.200 --> 01:20:18.720
and also when Joo
Young died, you were seen.

1024
01:20:18.760 --> 01:20:21.120
Now, everyone in the
world will see your face.

1025
01:20:21.200 --> 01:20:23.600
Everyone thought I lied.

1026
01:20:23.640 --> 01:20:24.920
But I'll show you all.

1027
01:20:25.280 --> 01:20:26.520
I'm faster than the news.

1028
01:20:26.880 --> 01:20:27.920
You see this guy?

1029
01:20:28.240 --> 01:20:30.640
And this guy, on the day Joo Young died.

1030
01:20:30.720 --> 01:20:32.680
You're here again, Mothman.

1031
01:20:33.240 --> 01:20:36.400
Now, it's time for you to run.

1032
01:20:38.600 --> 01:20:39.600
Catch him!

1033
01:20:39.680 --> 01:20:40.800
Stop!

1034
01:20:41.760 --> 01:20:42.760
Grab him!

1035
01:20:43.440 --> 01:20:44.600
You bastard!

1036
01:20:46.000 --> 01:20:47.680
Who are you? Where are you from?

1037
01:20:47.760 --> 01:20:49.000
I'm the president, you bastard!

1038
01:20:49.040 --> 01:20:50.696
You're afraid I'll
expose everything, right?

1039
01:20:50.720 --> 01:20:51.320
Where are you from?

1040
01:20:51.360 --> 01:20:53.920
President's Office? NSP? FBI? Spill it!

1041
01:20:56.560 --> 01:20:57.680
Let go!

1042
01:20:57.760 --> 01:20:58.760
Let me go!

1043
01:21:04.480 --> 01:21:05.480
Dad!

1044
01:21:06.160 --> 01:21:07.160
Hi.

1045
01:21:15.920 --> 01:21:19.280
Lee Chi-hyun is not a Sweeper.

1046
01:21:20.520 --> 01:21:22.400
You still think the Sweepers don't exist?

1047
01:21:22.480 --> 01:21:23.960
We only believe what we see.

1048
01:21:24.040 --> 01:21:27.160
I said we should stop when
Jackie went missing, you heard me.

1049
01:21:27.360 --> 01:21:28.920
Shouldn't we stop?

1050
01:21:29.960 --> 01:21:31.480
This is an accident, right?

1051
01:21:31.640 --> 01:21:33.120
Why would I kill Jeom-man?

1052
01:21:33.200 --> 01:21:34.200
You don't trust anyone.

1053
01:21:34.240 --> 01:21:36.480
You don't even try to. Am I wrong?

1054
01:21:42.160 --> 01:21:44.160
That must be the world we created, right?

1055
01:22:33.120 --> 01:22:34.200
Chi-hyun!

1056
01:22:35.280 --> 01:22:38.320
Darling! Oh no...

1057
01:22:38.480 --> 01:22:39.600
Please!

1058
01:22:40.480 --> 01:22:41.560
Chi-hyun!

1059
01:22:41.800 --> 01:22:42.800
Chi-hyun!

1060
01:22:43.520 --> 01:22:44.520
Please!

1061
01:22:44.600 --> 01:22:47.440
Darling, please... no!

1062
01:23:16.120 --> 01:23:18.960
This afternoon, a car accident took
place at Sangam crossroads.

1063
01:23:19.040 --> 01:23:22.800
An insurance agent in his
thirties named Lee was killed.

1064
01:23:23.200 --> 01:23:26.840
Lee's tragic accident occured while
crossing the street with his fiance,

1065
01:23:26.880 --> 01:23:29.320
who works as a journalist.

1066
01:23:39.720 --> 01:23:43.480
You mean Kang Dong-joon, Um Jae-man and you

1067
01:23:43.520 --> 01:23:44.760
all work together?

1068
01:23:49.280 --> 01:23:51.520
We did investigate Kang Dong-joon

1069
01:23:51.840 --> 01:23:54.080
because of Joo Young's death.

1070
01:23:54.400 --> 01:23:56.600
His mother was receiving
life-prolonging treatment.

1071
01:23:57.120 --> 01:23:59.720
We found a large sum of cash by his body.

1072
01:24:00.080 --> 01:24:05.160
He had no specific job,
but how'd he get that money?

1073
01:24:08.000 --> 01:24:12.440
Did you know her treatment
stopped after Mr. Kang died?

1074
01:24:18.800 --> 01:24:23.800
You committed numerous premeditated
murders including Mr. Joo's case.

1075
01:24:23.920 --> 01:24:26.240
And you want to come
clean. Is that correct?

1076
01:24:28.960 --> 01:24:29.960
Yes.

1077
01:24:31.760 --> 01:24:32.760
I see.

1078
01:24:34.480 --> 01:24:37.600
That's huge, but what should I do?

1079
01:24:37.680 --> 01:24:40.560
We closed all those
cases as accidental deaths.

1080
01:24:40.800 --> 01:24:42.720
The accidents are plotted.

1081
01:24:48.440 --> 01:24:50.200
Plotted accidents?

1082
01:24:51.720 --> 01:24:53.520
So, was it like this?

1083
01:24:55.600 --> 01:24:58.480
You calculate the exact
timing of rising sunshine,

1084
01:24:59.240 --> 01:25:02.200
and wait for Lee to
pass by at that exact time.

1085
01:25:02.800 --> 01:25:06.680
As a ray of sun reflects on the glass
hanging by the crane next to him,

1086
01:25:06.800 --> 01:25:09.560
it blocks the sight of the driver
coming from the other side,

1087
01:25:09.600 --> 01:25:11.960
causing him to hit Lee
Chi-hyun. Is that correct?

1088
01:25:12.640 --> 01:25:13.640
Yes.

1089
01:25:15.000 --> 01:25:16.280
Is that even possible?

1090
01:25:17.800 --> 01:25:19.400
I can reenact it.

1091
01:25:20.240 --> 01:25:23.280
Reenacting isn't important, evidence is.

1092
01:25:25.120 --> 01:25:29.760
To turn an accident into a crime,
you need evidence.

1093
01:25:30.240 --> 01:25:32.680
Go get evidence and come back.
I'll wait for you here.

1094
01:25:32.920 --> 01:25:34.280
I already told you.

1095
01:25:34.640 --> 01:25:36.320
It's all over the news, too.

1096
01:25:37.080 --> 01:25:39.840
The deceased, date of the accident,
circumstances of the accident.

1097
01:25:42.040 --> 01:25:43.720
You can check them.

1098
01:25:46.160 --> 01:25:50.240
No, for things like that,
you should tip off journalists.

1099
01:25:50.280 --> 01:25:51.800
This is a police station.

1100
01:25:52.440 --> 01:25:55.040
I can't believe what I'm hearing.

1101
01:25:56.200 --> 01:25:58.040
Did you check my background?

1102
01:25:59.880 --> 01:26:01.400
You must've got nothing.

1103
01:26:03.320 --> 01:26:05.160
You should go to therapy.

1104
01:26:05.400 --> 01:26:07.000
I killed all of them!

1105
01:26:09.560 --> 01:26:11.200
Why don't you believe what I say?

1106
01:26:12.880 --> 01:26:14.960
Should I believe everything you say?

1107
01:26:15.280 --> 01:26:16.320
Then...

1108
01:26:19.520 --> 01:26:21.160
what do you think I am?

1109
01:26:22.080 --> 01:26:24.520
We caught this nutcase today.

1110
01:26:25.360 --> 01:26:27.776
He took over the broadcasting station
and aired conspiracy theories.

1111
01:26:27.800 --> 01:26:29.480
He's delusional.

1112
01:26:32.440 --> 01:26:34.560
We get plenty of people like you.

1113
01:26:35.120 --> 01:26:36.640
And you're late.

1114
01:26:36.800 --> 01:26:40.480
Someone just called us saying
he killed Joo Sung-jik.

1115
01:26:40.720 --> 01:26:44.560
The police have no time
to investigate such claims.

1116
01:26:45.320 --> 01:26:47.120
We've no time for that.

1117
01:26:49.560 --> 01:26:54.680
Do you really think the Sweepers exist?

1118
01:27:00.560 --> 01:27:02.080
I'm really quitting now.

1119
01:27:03.520 --> 01:27:05.640
I want to live a normal life.

1120
01:27:07.720 --> 01:27:09.280
You understand, right?

1121
01:27:16.120 --> 01:27:18.560
You think it's safe to leave here?

1122
01:27:21.920 --> 01:27:23.200
What do you mean?

1123
01:27:25.240 --> 01:27:27.840
I found a wiretap in our office.

1124
01:27:36.360 --> 01:27:38.880
Sweepers? What's that?

1125
01:27:39.000 --> 01:27:41.240
Plotters who are bigger than us.

1126
01:27:42.360 --> 01:27:45.600
Plotters are after us?

1127
01:27:46.440 --> 01:27:50.200
Back then... I wanted
to keep hold of Odd Eye.

1128
01:27:50.280 --> 01:27:52.320
Wait till I figure things out.

1129
01:28:17.520 --> 01:28:21.280
Do you really think the Sweepers exist?

1130
01:28:21.800 --> 01:28:23.320
Among so many accidents,

1131
01:28:23.720 --> 01:28:26.040
there are surely some that were plotted.

1132
01:28:26.880 --> 01:28:28.400
I am the evidence.

1133
01:28:28.480 --> 01:28:29.680
We're heading out.

1134
01:28:29.760 --> 01:28:31.080
Okay, proceed with that.

1135
01:28:31.760 --> 01:28:34.040
So, tell me more about the Sweepers.

1136
01:28:34.320 --> 01:28:36.120
To plot an accident...

1137
01:28:36.480 --> 01:28:39.600
they must have a job
highly accessible to accidents.

1138
01:28:41.040 --> 01:28:44.360
If you're right, you
really can't trust anyone.

1139
01:28:47.800 --> 01:28:51.480
Can you believe me, a cop?

1140
01:29:35.360 --> 01:29:40.600
A pedestrian crossing the
intersection and a sedan collided.

1141
01:29:40.800 --> 01:29:44.920
It was revealed that the car, which was
driving, did not see the signal and rushed in.

1142
01:29:45.040 --> 01:29:49.000
Three pedestrians crossing
the intersection died on the spot.

1143
01:29:49.040 --> 01:29:52.680
A man in his 30s, an insurance
company employee, Mr. Lee, passed away.

1144
01:29:52.720 --> 01:29:55.296
It was reported that he was crossing
the street with his fiancée...

1145
01:29:55.320 --> 01:30:00.240
A man who fell 8 meters from his balcony,
was fortunately not injured.

1146
01:30:00.280 --> 01:30:02.280
Due to a malfunction in
the building's fire alarm,

1147
01:30:02.320 --> 01:30:05.520
the sprinklers activated, causing a sudden
increase in water pressure...

1148
01:30:05.600 --> 01:30:10.880
The police restored and released the
bus's black box footage to the media.

1149
01:30:10.920 --> 01:30:13.880
Breaking news: Today, the newly appointed
candidate for the Prosecutor

1150
01:30:13.920 --> 01:30:15.360
General, Mr. Joo, has passed away.

1151
01:30:15.400 --> 01:30:19.240
The cause of the accident is presumed to be an
electrical leakage from broadcasting equipment.

1152
01:30:19.280 --> 01:30:22.960
It has been reported that
the bus did not slow down

1153
01:30:23.000 --> 01:30:25.280
and ran over people on the crosswalk.

1154
01:30:25.320 --> 01:30:27.920
The incident is being investigated
with "black ice,"

1155
01:30:27.960 --> 01:30:31.440
also known as the phenomenon
of sudden icing, as a likely cause.

1156
01:30:31.480 --> 01:30:33.816
An investigation is underway to determine
whether Mr. Han, who is 180cm tall,

1157
01:30:33.840 --> 01:30:37.216
was able to commit suicide from a towel rack
located more than 20cm below his height...

1158
01:30:37.240 --> 01:30:42.000
Mr. Kim lost his balance and fell 20 meters
down the escalator at the station.

1159
01:30:42.040 --> 01:30:44.440
Mr. Kim's cellphone
disappeared from the scene,

1160
01:30:44.480 --> 01:30:46.800
and the accident video confirmed...

1161
01:30:46.880 --> 01:30:49.496
Mr. Kim Kyu-chul, who was under investigation
for embezzlement and misappropriation,

1162
01:30:49.520 --> 01:30:51.696
gained fame on his personal
social media by showcasing...

1163
01:30:51.720 --> 01:30:54.960
A vehicle fell from the
5th floor of a building you see there.

1164
01:30:55.040 --> 01:30:58.920
According to eyewitnesses, it crashed
through the railing and fell straight down.

1165
01:31:05.640 --> 01:31:10.680
The Plot
